# Phase 8: Calculate the post-hoc 100% recall point

This is probably the most interesting descriptive statistic for the blog post.

Among the 15 or so studies that were ultimately included, find:

```text
minimum Jev probability
```

This is effectively the highest threshold that can still retain every ultimately included record.

Then report:

```text
Post-hoc threshold required for 100% recall
Number of included studies retained
Number of included studies missed
Number of all records retained for human screening
Number of records automatically excluded
Workload reduction %
```

Label this clearly:

**Post-hoc/oracle 100%-recall threshold**

Explain that it was determined using the known labels and therefore measures how separable the records were according to Jev. It is NOT a threshold that could have been selected prospectively without validation data.

Also calculate the analogous threshold achieving at least:

```text
95% recall
```

if meaningful given the small number of positive cases.

